 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Memory:** The lookup table is an `ARRAY2D` of `Color` objects. Memory usage scales with the product of the X and Y axis resolutions (image width $\times$ height). This is generally larger than two separate 1D LUTs if the 2D function is separable, but necessary for non-separable mappings [S2].
-*   **Performance:** Rendering requires a 2D texture lookup per sample. This is computationally more expensive than 1D lookup but allows for richer classification [S1, unofficial].
